  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "description": "This Red Hat Security Advisory addresses multiple vulnerabilities, bug fixes, and enhancements in the Linux kernel packages for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.2 Extended Update Support. The update includes fixes for various security issues such as out-of-bounds reads, heap overflows, use-after-free bugs, integer overflows, and information leaks across different kernel subsystems including networking, Bluetooth, filesystem encryption, Wi-Fi, SCSI, DRM, and others. The advisory emphasizes the importance of applying these kernel updates and rebooting the system to ensure the fixes take effect.",
